      "The day-21 fallback lacks a capacity-constrained stock and shortfall calculation. Assuming capacity is expressed in complete sets and a 30-day planning month, 21 days at 2,500/month yields about 1,750 sets, against approximately 560 sets of concurrent demand—only about 1,190 additional sets before existing inventory. The plan should reconcile this with the 4,000–5,000-set bridge objective and identify the uncovered period. Existing stock, ramp readiness and alternative purchases remain unverified.",
      "The tooling-transfer schedule is not coordinated with the proposed LPI production bridge. Moving the plastic tooling on days 21–46 could prevent LPI from making subsequent complete lamps. Release should be gated on sufficient completed stock, a validated alternative plastics arrangement, or another agreed production solution; the local development schedule should reflect actual tooling availability.",
